--   VAT return form (worksheet 32a, standard rate): sections A to E, output tax, input tax and the VAT payable or credit (the copy online still prints 7.5 %; its line numbers are those of the guidance on completing the return) (Department of Inland Revenue, Commonwealth of The Bahamas)
--     https://inlandrevenue.finance.gov.bs/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/VAT-Form-No.-32a-Return-Filing-Worksheet-Standard-Rate-v2.4_20141216-edited.pdf
--   VAT Guidance on Completing a VAT Return, standard method (version of 1 January 2017): lines 1 to 31 of the return, still printing the 7.5 % rate of that year (Department of Inland Revenue, Commonwealth of The Bahamas)
--     https://inlandrevenue.finance.gov.bs/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/2017-01-01-VAT-Guidance-on-Completing-a-VAT-Return.pdf
--   Payment – VAT: the return and the payment are due within 21 days after the end of the VAT period, filed online (Department of Inland Revenue, Commonwealth of The Bahamas)
--     https://inlandrevenue.finance.gov.bs/value-added-tax/payment-vat/
--   Value Added Tax — the Department's VAT pages (legal texts, forms, payment, FAQs); the online filing service is vat.revenue.gov.bs (Department of Inland Revenue, Commonwealth of The Bahamas)
--     https://inlandrevenue.finance.gov.bs/value-added-tax/
